          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most homes, the right stud finder setup costs well under $75: a Franklin multi-sensor array for drywall plus a CH Hanson magnet for plaster, tile and second opinions. Together they locate framing faster, and with fewer false readings, than the single-sensor tools most of us grew up using.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Move up to a Zircon or Bosch scanner when wire and metal detection matter for your work, and to a Walabot only when you are planning a renovation. Whatever tool is in your hand, scan at more than one height, confirm with a test hole, stay clear of the zone above and below outlets, and put heavy loads into wood.
          </p>
